{
  "name": "cloud_volume_matrix",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§25c and §25d against each other and against §25b, at the sunset elevation both exist for (issue #144). A 2x2 RATHER THAN AN A/B, and the reason is a measurement. §25c's raymarch and §25b's bake were shot at this same elevation and differed by a mean of 0.19/255 with not one pixel moving by more than 2 — which reads as 'the renderer does nothing' and is not what it means. §25b couples the sheet's alpha to how lit the ground is, so a sunlit deck at -2.44 degrees lands near 0.075 effective alpha over near-black terrain: there is barely any cloud drawn for EITHER renderer to render. One flag each separates the two claims, and only the fourth frame is the thing #144 asks for. Hour and elevation are measured, not chosen: 20.86 h is where cloud_deck_varieties.json pins sun_elevation at -2.4417, and that elevation is pinned here beside it so a clock change fails loudly instead of quietly emptying the frames.",
